<title>USA: US banks free reserves $1.479 bln Jan 1 rvsd 2 wk.</title>
<headline>US banks free reserves $1.479 bln Jan 1 rvsd 2 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $1.479 billion per day in the two weeks ended January 1, versus revised free reserves of $1,320 billion in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $64 million versus $67 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
